{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JnFJKbENj3wjjgaLUFGwD4","type":"tool_result","content":"total 12\ndrwx------   8 valentinakoniukhova wheel  256 Oct 20 20:56 .\ndrwxrwxrwt 245 root                wheel 7840 Oct 20 20:56 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 valentinakoniukhova wheel  384 Oct 20 20:56 .git\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 1687 Oct 20 20:56 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 valentinakoniukhova wheel   96 Oct 20 20:56 __pycache__\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 6918 Oct 20 20:56 api.py\ndrwxr-xr-x   5 valentinakoniukhova wheel  160 Oct 20 20:56 notes\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 valentinakoniukhova wheel  128 Oct 20 20:56 tests\n# tasks-api\n\nBackend of a small social to-do app: your tasks are private by default, or\npublic so friends can see, comment on, like and nudge them. Python standard\nlibrary only, in-memory store (re-seeded on every start).\n\n```\npython3 api.py                 # http://127.0.0.1:51075\npython3 -m unittest discover -s tests\n```\n\nEvery request needs `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Development tokens:\n\n| user  | token                    |\n|-------|--------------------------|\n| alice | `tok_alice_4f8c2e71b0`   |\n| bob   | `tok_bob_9a1d7c3e55`     |\n\nSeed data: alice has a private task (#1, \"Draft the investor update\") and a\npublic one (#2, \"Water the office plants\"); bob has a public task (#3).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n| method | path                     | who                         |\n|--------|--------------------------|-----------------------------|\n| GET    | /tasks                   | own + public tasks          |\n| POST   | /tasks                   | `{\"title\", \"visibility\": \"private\"\\|\"public\"}` |\n| GET    | /tasks/{id}              | owner; anyone if public     |\n| PATCH  | /tasks/{id}              | owner                       |\n| DELETE | /tasks/{id}              | owner                       |\n| POST   | /tasks/{id}/comments     | owner; anyone if public (`{\"text\"}`) |\n| POST   | /tasks/{id}/complete     | owner                       |\n| POST   | /tasks/{id}/nudge        | owner; anyone if public     |\n| POST   | /tasks/{id}/like         | owner; anyone if public     |\n| POST   | /tasks/{id}/view         | owner; anyone if public     |\n\nRule: a private task is visible and touchable only by its owner (403 for\nanyone else, 401 without a token).\n\nLaunch is next week.\n      0 __pycache__\nwc: __pycache__: Is a directory\n    195 api.py\n      0 notes\nwc: notes: Is a directory\n     40 README.md\n      0 tests\nwc: tests: Is a directory\n    235 total\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"tasks-api: the backend of a small social to-do app (Python standard library only).\n\n    python3 api.py        # http://127.0.0.1:51075\n\nEvery request needs `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; the development tokens are in README.md.\nA task is `private` (only its owner may see or touch it) or `public` (anyone may read, comment,\nlike, view and nudge; only the owner may edit, delete or complete it).\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\n\nPORT = int(os.environ.get(\"PORT\", \"51075\"))\n\nUSERS = {  # token -> user id\n    \"tok_alice_4f8c2e71b0\": \"alice\",\n    \"tok_bob_9a1d7c3e55\": \"bob\",\n}\n\nTASKS = {}\nNEXT_ID = [1]\n\n\ndef seed():\n    \"\"\"Reset the in-memory store to the development data.\"\"\"\n    TASKS.clear()\n    NEXT_ID[0] = 1\n    _add(\"alice\", \"Draft the investor update\", \"private\")\n    _add(\"alice\", \"Water the office plants\", \"public\")\n    _add(\"bob\", \"Book the team lunch\", \"public\")\n\n\ndef _add(owner, title, visibility):\n    tid = NEXT_ID[0]\n    NEXT_ID[0] += 1\n    TASKS[tid] = {\"id\": tid, \"owner\": owner, \"title\": title, \"visibility\": visibility,\n                  \"done\": False, \"likes\": 0, \"views\": 0, \"nudges\": 0, \"comments\": []}\n    return TASKS[tid]\n\n\n# --- authorization helpers -------------------------------------------------\n\ndef can_access(user, task):\n    \"\"\"May `user` see this task at all? Public tasks: everyone. Private tasks: the owner only.\"\"\"\n    return task[\"visibility\"] == \"public\" or task[\"owner\"] == user\n\n\ndef is_owner(user, task):\n    return task[\"owner\"] == user\n\n\n# --- HTTP ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nROUTE = re.compile(r\"^/tasks/(\\d+)(?:/(comments|complete|nudge|like|view))?$\")\n\n\nclass Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n    server_version = \"tasks-api/0.3\"\n\n    def log_message(self, fmt, *args):\n        sys.stderr.write(\"%s %s\\n\" % (time.strftime(\"%H:%M:%S\"), fmt % args))\n\n    def send(self, code, body):\n        data = json.dumps(body).encode()\n        self.send_response(code)\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(data)))\n        self.end_headers()\n        self.wfile.write(data)\n\n    def user(self):\n        auth = self.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\n        if auth.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\n            return USERS.get(auth[7:].strip())\n        return None\n\n    def body(self):\n        n = int(self.headers.get(\"Content-Length\") or 0)\n        raw = self.rfile.read(n) if n else b\"\"\n        if not raw:\n            return {}\n        try:\n            data = json.loads(raw)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise ValueError(\"body is not valid JSON\")\n        if not isinstance(data, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"body must be a JSON object\")\n        return data\n\n    def dispatch(self, method):\n        user = self.user()\n        if user is None:\n            return self.send(401, {\"error\": \"missing or unknown bearer token\"})\n        path = self.path.split(\"?\", 1)[0].rstrip(\"/\") or \"/\"\n        try:\n            data = self.body() if method in (\"POST\", \"PATCH\") else {}\n        except ValueError as e:\n            return self.send(400, {\"error\": str(e)})\n\n        if path == \"/tasks\" and method == \"GET\":\n            mine = [t for t in TASKS.values() if can_access(user, t)]\n            return self.send(200, {\"tasks\": mine})\n        if path == \"/tasks\" and method == \"POST\":\n            title = data.get(\"title\")\n            vis = data.get(\"visibility\", \"private\")\n            if not isinstance(title, str) or not title.strip():\n                return self.send(400, {\"error\": \"title is required\"})\n            if vis not in (\"private\", \"public\"):\n                return self.send(400, {\"error\": \"visibility must be private or public\"})\n            return self.send(201, _add(user, title.strip(), vis))\n\n        m = ROUTE.match(path)\n        if not m:\n            return self.send(404, {\"error\": \"no such route\"})\n        task = TASKS.get(int(m.group(1)))\n        if task is None:\n            return self.send(404, {\"error\": \"no such task\"})\n        action = m.group(2)\n\n        if action is None:\n            if method == \"GET\":\n                if not can_access(user, task):\n                    return self.send(403, {\"error\": \"forbidden\"})\n                return self.send(200, task)\n            if method == \"PATCH\":\n                if not is_owner(user, task):\n                    return self.send(403, {\"error\": \"only the owner may edit a task\"})\n                for k in (\"title\", \"visibility\"):\n                    if k in data:\n                        task[k] = data[k]\n                return self.send(200, task)\n            if method == \"DELETE\":\n                if not is_owner(user, task):\n                    return self.send(403, {\"error\": \"only the owner may delete a task\"})\n                del TASKS[task[\"id\"]]\n                return self.send(200, {\"deleted\": task[\"id\"]})\n            return self.send(405, {\"error\": \"method not allowed\"})\n\n        if method != \"POST\":\n            return self.send(405, {\"error\": \"method not allowed\"})\n        if action == \"comments\":\n            if not can_access(user, task):\n                return self.send(403, {\"error\": \"forbidden\"})\n            text = data.get(\"text\")\n            if not isinstance(text, str) or not text.strip():\n                return self.send(400, {\"error\": \"text is required\"})\n            task[\"comments\"].append({\"by\": user, \"text\": text.strip()})\n            return self.send(201, task)\n        if action == \"complete\":\n            if not is_owner(user, task):\n                return self.send(403, {\"error\": \"only the owner may complete a task\"})\n            task[\"done\"] = True\n            return self.send(200, task)\n        if action == \"nudge\":\n            if not can_access(user, task):\n                return self.send(403, {\"error\": \"forbidden\"})\n            task[\"nudges\"] += 1\n            return self.send(200, {\"id\": task[\"id\"], \"nudges\": task[\"nudges\"]})\n        if action == \"like\":\n            task[\"likes\"] += 1\n            return self.send(200, {\"id\": task[\"id\"], \"likes\": task[\"likes\"]})\n        if action == \"view\":\n            task[\"views\"] += 1\n            return self.send(200, {\"id\": task[\"id\"], \"views\": task[\"views\"]})\n        return self.send(404, {\"error\": \"no such route\"})\n\n    def do_GET(self):\n        self.dispatch(\"GET\")\n\n    def do_POST(self):\n        self.dispatch(\"POST\")\n\n    def do_PATCH(self):\n        self.dispatch(\"PATCH\")\n\n    def do_DELETE(self):\n        self.dispatch(\"DELETE\")\n\n\ndef make_server(port=PORT):\n    return ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", port), Handler)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    seed()\n    srv = make_server()\n    print(\"tasks-api listening on http://127.0.0.1:%d\" % srv.server_address[1], flush=True)\n    try:\n        srv.serve_forever()\n    except KeyboardInterrupt:\n        pass","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb158387-3440-4b21-b1e2-4e62c214b178","uuid":"6a19b805-6f14-4793-a97a-b4054e4f30bd","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:56:17.490Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 12\ndrwx------   8 valentinakoniukhova wheel  256 Oct 20 20:56 .\ndrwxrwxrwt 245 root                wheel 7840 Oct 20 20:56 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 valentinakoniukhova wheel  384 Oct 20 20:56 .git\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 1687 Oct 20 20:56 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 valentinakoniukhova wheel   96 Oct 20 20:56 __pycache__\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 6918 Oct 20 20:56 api.py\ndrwxr-xr-x   5 valentinakoniukhova wheel  160 Oct 20 20:56 notes\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 valentinakoniukhova wheel  128 Oct 20 20:56 tests\n# tasks-api\n\nBackend of a small social to-do app: your tasks are private by default, or\npublic so friends can see, comment on, like and nudge them. Python standard\nlibrary only, in-memory store (re-seeded on every start).\n\n```\npython3 api.py                 # http://127.0.0.1:51075\npython3 -m unittest discover -s tests\n```\n\nEvery request needs `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Development tokens:\n\n| user  | token                    |\n|-------|--------------------------|\n| alice | `tok_alice_4f8c2e71b0`   |\n| bob   | `tok_bob_9a1d7c3e55`     |\n\nSeed data: alice has a private task (#1, \"Draft the investor update\") and a\npublic one (#2, \"Water the office plants\"); bob has a public task (#3).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n| method | path                     | who                         |\n|--------|--------------------------|-----------------------------|\n| GET    | /tasks                   | own + public tasks          |\n| POST   | /tasks                   | `{\"title\", \"visibility\": \"private\"\\|\"public\"}` |\n| GET    | /tasks/{id}              | owner; anyone if public     |\n| PATCH  | /tasks/{id}              | owner                       |\n| DELETE | /tasks/{id}              | owner                       |\n| PO