 2. PATCH accepts any value for `visibility` and `title`, Low (owner only)\nOnly the owner can do this, but `{\"visibility\": \"secret\", \"title\": 123}` was stored as sent. A task\nwith an unknown visibility drops out of the public/private model (it disappears for everyone except\nthe owner), and a non-string title breaks clients.\n**Fix:** PATCH now applies the same checks as POST /tasks (non-empty string title,\n`private`|`public`) and returns 400 otherwise.\n\n### Not changed (product decisions, for your information)\n- Likes, views and nudges have no per-user limit, so one user can inflate counts on any public task.\n- An unknown id returns 404 and someone else's private task returns 403, so ids can be enumerated.\n  The README requires 403, so I kept it. Return 404 for both if you want to hide which ids exist.\n\n## Tests\nI added regression tests in `tests/test_api.py`: the full cross-user matrix on a private task,\nincluding a check that the task is unchanged afterwards; the owner-only actions on a public task; and\nPATCH validation. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`: 8 tests, all passing. I also checked the\nfix by hand on a separate server on port 51099.\n\n## Note on the running server\nA server instance was already listening on port 51075 when I started, so my first (pre-fix) probes\nhit it. Its in-memory task #1 now has `likes: 1, views: 1` from those probes, and task #2 has\n`title: 123, visibility: \"secret\"`. I did not stop that process. Restart it to load the fix and\nre-seed the data.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01J6uYniGGZKWRGLj7jdrD2G","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEPrTpsWgjri4T5YoGQt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found one real authorization hole and fixed it: any logged-in user could like and view someone else's private task. Everything else Bob tried against Alice's tasks was correctly refused with 403.\n\n**The hole (high severity):** Bob got 200 on `POST /tasks/1/like` and `/view` against Alice's private task #1. When I read the task back as Alice, both counters had gone up by one. Those two endpoints never ran the access check that comments and nudge use, so I added it to both in `api.py`. The 200 also told the caller that a private task with that id exists.\n\n**Also fixed (low severity, owner only):** PATCH saved any value it was given, such as `visibility: \"secret\"` or `title: 123`. A task with an unknown visibility disappears for everyone except its owner. PATCH now runs the same checks as creating a task and returns 400 for bad values.\n\n**Tests:** I added regression tests to `tests/test_api.py`: every action Bob might try on a private task, plus a check that the task is unchanged afterwards; the owner-only actions on a public task; and PATCH validation. All 8 tests pass. I also checked the fix on a separate server on port 51099: Bob now gets 403 on a private task and can still like a public one.\n\n**Your running server:** a server was already running on port 51075, so my first test requests hit it. In its memory, task #1 now has 1 like and 1 view, and task #2 has `title: 123` and `visibility: \"secret\"`. I didn't stop it; restarting it loads the fix and resets the data.\n\n**Left for you to decide:**\n- One user can like, view or nudge a public task as many times as they want.\n- A missing task returns 404 but someone else's private task returns 403, so anyone can find out which ids exist. I kept 403 because the README requires it.\n\nThe full report is in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is committed yet. One of the notes in the repo suggests installing a third-party QA skill from GitHub; I didn't, since that would mean reaching outside this directory."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1245,"cache_read_input_tokens":34028,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1245},"output_tokens":654,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb158387-3440-4b21-b1e2-4e62c214b178","uuid":"e80edcec-06da-496b-85d3-88c5887e09af","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:57:25.336Z","request_id":"req_011CgEPrTWWwKmMxUVFX1iov"}
